-- title:
--   Finite type of the full-level fine moduli ring over A₀
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\neq q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$, and let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by $q$ and which contains a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity, with $\ell$ and $M'$ units in $A_0$. Assume moreover: the predicates [`ModularCurve.IsLevelPStructure`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelP.html#L104) at $\ell$ (a pair of affine points $P,Q$ on $W$ satisfying the Weierstrass equation, annihilated by $W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$, and with both independence elements units) and [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55) at prime powers (a cyclic-kernel or two-kernel divisor condition on a polynomial) are preserved by Weierstrass variable change, via the prescribed actions on level data and on kernel polynomials; a family $\mathcal G$ of relative group laws on the projective models over all $A_0$-algebras which is chord–tangent (its points functor is compatible with addition and Galois twisting) and has the origin as identity; a level transport $\mathcal T$ of raw Drinfeld pairs which is a section transport, i.e. compatible with the graded variable-change and coefficient homomorphisms on projective models; and the existence, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, of such graded homomorphisms $\varphi$ for variable changes and for coefficient maps, each with the irrelevant ideal condition. Let $P_0$ be any abstract fine moduli package for the level moduli datum attached to the rigid Weierstrass datum $\Gamma_0(M')\times\Gamma(\ell)\times$ Drinfeld-$\Gamma(q)$ formed from these data, that is, an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ together with a universal point over $B_0$ such that every point over every $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of the universal one under a unique $A_0$-algebra map $B_0\to T$. Then $B_0$ is a finitely generated $A_0$-algebra.
--
--   This records that the fine moduli ring of the rigidified full-level problem over the unramified base $A_0$ is of finite type, the form in which finiteness is needed when the moduli ring is analysed modulo the maximal ideal. It is used in the integrality and irreducibility argument for the quotient of the moduli ring by the ideal generated by $j$ minus a specified value.
